# I-Spy: a text guessing game (live)

A tiny round-based "I spy with my little eye…" game that runs in the live
editor's text transcript. It shows the `%cli-live` target and `wchntConsole`:
`%init` prints the first clue once, and `%step(line)` answers each guess you
type.

The Game holds a list of `Thing`s, the index of the current secret, how many
you have found, the last reply, and a shared `@WCHNTMaths` handle so rounds
pick a new secret at random.

## Schema

```
Game = [Thing]/things Int/secret Int/found String/msg @WCHNTMaths/maths
Thing = String/name String/clue
```

## Construction

```
apple =    [:Thing "apple" "something red and round"].
bicycle =  [:Thing "bicycle" "something with two wheels"].
clock =    [:Thing "clock" "something that tells the time"].
book =     [:Thing "book" "something with pages"].

[:Game [:Array/Thing apple bicycle clock book] 0 0 "" maths]
```

## Methods

```
Thing::clueLine = {
  "I spy with my little eye, {clue}.".tpl({String:String "clue": clue})
}

Game::secretThing = { things.get(secret) }

Game::nextSecretId = { Int/oldId |
  r = maths.randInt(things.length() - 1).
  if (r >= oldId) { r + 1 } else { r }
}

Game::start = {
  first = maths.randInt(things.length()).
  t = things.get(first).
  [:Game | secret = first, msg = t.clueLine()]
}

Game::onFound = { Thing/t |
  next = this.nextSecretId(secret).
  nt = things.get(next).
  count = found + 1.
  win = "Yes! You found the {name}! ({count} so far)".tpl({String:String "name": t.name, "count": count.str()}).
  [:Game | secret = next, found = count, msg = win.concat(" ").concat(nt.clueLine())]
}

Game::onMiss = { String/line |
  [:Game | msg = "No, not {guess}. Try again.".tpl({String:String "guess": line})]
}

Game::guess = { String/line |
  t = this.secretThing().
  if (line == t.name) { this.onFound(t) } else { this.onMiss(line) }
}
```

## Target

```
%cli-live

%requires
WCHNTMaths::randInt(Int) -> Int

%init
var game;

function init() {
    game = GameAssemblage.factory(wchntMaths);
    wchntConsole.println("I spy with my little eye… type a guess and press Enter.");
    game = game.start();
    wchntConsole.println(game.msg);
}

%step
function step(line) {
    game = game.guess(line);
    wchntConsole.println(game.msg);
}
```
